# Local source-study clones are development references only (not product code).
#
# These are the glob families named in the binding exclusion checklist
# (docs/UPSTREAM_REFERENCES.md): _references*, .upstreams*, labcairn-upstreams*.
# An earlier version listed the bare directory names, which left _references_old/
# and labcairn-upstreams-cache/ untracked-but-visible, and therefore packable.
#
# Case variants are spelled out deliberately. The development machine runs
# core.ignorecase=true; a Linux CI runner does not. A lowercase-only pattern
# silently stops matching there, so the exclusion would hold on the laptop and
# fail in the build that actually publishes. Verified with
# `git -c core.ignorecase=false check-ignore`.
_references*
.upstreams*
labcairn-upstreams*
_REFERENCES*
.UPSTREAMS*
LABCAIRN-UPSTREAMS*
_References*
.Upstreams*
LabCairn-upstreams*
labcairn-Upstreams*
LabCairn-Upstreams*

# Basics for the planned Python and frontend projects
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
node_modules/
web/dist/
.DS_Store

# Build and packaging output. These are reproducible from source at any time,
# and shipping them would defeat the clean-venv install check in LC-P1-01.
# `git add -A` must never be able to stage a wheel.
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
archive/
.wheel-check/
coverage/
web/coverage/
